Version 1.1
===========

* Read input from pipes. For example, to count DNA from zipped files, run:

% gunzip -c *.fa.gz | jellyfish [options] /dev/fd/0

* Support fasta and fastq formats.

* count --presence-only: only record the presence of k-mers (1 bit
  counter in memory, k-mers already seen are not incremented).
  --out-counter-len still sets the width of the counter field in the
  output.

* merge --free-inputs: release the disk space of the input files as
  they are consumed and delete them on success, so merging needs
  little more than the size of the final database (Linux only; the
  inputs are unusable if merge fails).

* Support for counting 'q-mers', as defined by the Quake error
  correcting software (http://www.cbcb.umd.edu/software/quake/).

* New dump subcommands which replaces 'stats -f' and 'stats -c'.
